### Why is async decoupling essential?

A producer like the transfer service publishes a notification event to a queue and returns immediately. Consumers do the slow work of calling external providers. A slow SMS gateway never slows a money transfer.

```java
package com.bank.notification;

public class TransferNotificationPublisher {
    public void onTransferCompleted(Transfer t) {
        notificationQueue.publish(new NotificationEvent(
            t.accountId(), NotificationType.TRANSFER_SUCCESS,
            Map.of("amount", t.amount().toString(), "to", t.toAccount()),
            Priority.HIGH));
    }
}
```

### How does channel selection work?

Each user record stores which channels they opted into. The system respects do-not-disturb windows and regulatory opt-outs.

```java
package com.bank.notification;

public class ChannelSelector {
    public List<Channel> select(String userId, NotificationType type) {
        UserPreferences prefs = prefStore.get(userId);
        if (prefs.isDoNotDisturb()) return List.of();
        return prefs.channelsFor(type); // e.g., [PUSH, SMS]
    }
}
```

### How does template rendering work?

A template engine fills placeholders with event data, keeping messages consistent and translatable.

```java
package com.bank.notification;

public class TemplateRenderer {
    public String render(String templateId, Map<String, String> data) {
        String template = templateStore.get(templateId);
        // "Dear {name}, Rs.{amount} transferred to {to}"
        for (var entry : data.entrySet())
            template = template.replace("{" + entry.getKey() + "}", entry.getValue());
        return template;
    }
}
```

### How does priority handling work?

Critical messages like fraud alerts use a high-priority queue that is consumed first. Marketing messages use a low-priority queue that yields to security alerts.

### How does retry logic work?

Retry transient failures with exponential backoff. After max attempts, move to a dead-letter queue for investigation.

```java
package com.bank.notification;

public class RetryHandler {
    public void handleWithRetry(NotificationEvent event) {
        if (event.attempts() >= MAX_RETRIES) {
            deadLetterQueue.send(event);
            return;
        }
        try { deliver(event); }
        catch (Exception e) {
            retryQueue.sendWithDelay(event.incrementAttempts(),
                backoff(event.attempts()));
        }
    }
}
```

### How do you ensure idempotent delivery?

Each notification carries a stable id. The dispatcher records delivered ids, so a redelivery is recognized and the customer is never texted twice.

### How do you track delivery status?

Track at each stage: queued, sent, delivered, failed. This gives operations visibility into notification health.

### What should a senior engineer know?

A senior engineer designs for provider failover (primary SMS provider down, fall back to secondary), monitors delivery rates and latency by channel, and ensures notifications comply with regulatory requirements like opt-out handling.
